stook:
n. A small collection of sheaves set up in the field; a shock;
in England, twelve sheaves.
v. t. To set up, as sheaves of grain, in stooks.

strath:
n. A valley of considerable size, through which a river runs;
adj. valley bottom; -- often used in composition with the name of the
river; as, Strath Spey, Strathdon, Strathmore.
